## 3. Architecture Assessment

### 3.1 Strengths

- **Clean component decomposition.** Each section is a single-purpose file; `App.tsx` is just composition.
- **Typed content model.** `content.ts` exports explicit interfaces (`Cafe`, `Hangout`, `SocialEvent`, `RelaxationSpot`, `RoastTemplate`) — no `any` leaking.
- **Reusable animation hook.** `useScrollAnimation` is generic (`<T extends HTMLElement>`) and consistently applied across sections.
- **Consistent design system.** Custom Tailwind color ramps (`chai`, `ember`, `leaf`), three font families, and a shared utilities layer (`card-hover`, `glass`, `text-balance`).
- **Accessibility basics present.** Mobile menu has `aria-label`/`aria-expanded`, scroll-down link has `aria-label`, form inputs have `htmlFor`/`id` pairs, `noValidate` on the form.
- **Safe external links.** `target="_blank"` anchors use `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- **Responsive.** Mobile-first layouts with `sm:`/`md:`/`lg:` breakpoints throughout.

### 3.2 Weaknesses & Risks

| # | Severity | Area | Finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Medium | Data | All content is hardcoded; no persistence. A Supabase instance is provisioned but unused. If the user expects SOS submissions to be saved, they currently are not — the form only flips a local `submitted` flag. |
| 2 | Low | Geolocation | `handleDetectLocation` in `Cafes.tsx` requests the position but discards the coordinates — it only sets status to `'success'`. No distance re-sorting or map intent uses the result, so the feature is cosmetic. |
| 3 | Low | Accessibility | No `<main>` landmark issues (it exists), but several icon-only buttons (e.g. the roast toggle in `CafeCard`, the copy button in `RoastGenerator`) rely on icons without `aria-label`. The copy button has one; the roast toggle does not. |
| 4 | Low | SEO | `index.html` references `/vite.svg` as favicon but no such file exists in the project (it's the default Vite template value). Will 404 in production. |
| 5 | Low | Meta | `og:image` and `twitter:image` point at `bolt.new/static/og_default.png` — a generic placeholder, not project-specific. |
| 6 | Info | Bundle | `lucide-react` is excluded from `optimizeDeps` in `vite.config.ts`. This is fine for dev but means the entire icon set is processed at build; tree-shaking should still handle it, but worth verifying bundle size. |
| 7 | Info | Unused code | `parseLow` regex extracts the first `₹N` from price ranges — works for the current data shape but would silently return `0` for any range without a leading rupee figure, skewing sort. Low risk given controlled data. |
| 8 | Info | Key prop | `SocialLife` and `RoastGenerator` use array index as `key` (`key={i}`). Fine for static lists but fragile if the data becomes dynamic. |
| 9 | Info | `Footer` | A `Github` icon is imported from lucide-react but never rendered — dead import. |

